00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.630 align:start position:0%
human beings flourish  when they have power to direct the  course of their own life  the best way to have access to that  power is through participation in a  constitutional democracy  but democracy survives only if its  citizens  know how to participate  want to participate have the skills to  participate  constitutional democracy is a living  activity not something simply to learn  about on paper  this isn't an old-fashioned civics class  where you learn a bunch of information  about things that are distant from your  life  this is about putting yourself as a  learner in the position of an  active civic participant who needs to  know what you care about and how things  work  in order to shape your own civic journey  we'll still cover the traditional  disciplinary content think separation of  powers and checks and balances  you'll need to learn about rights and  responsibilities constitutionalism  the philosophical foundations of  democracy and the levers of change  but we will also ask you to put your  learning  into action you'll work from your  understanding of yourself  and your understanding of constitutional  democracy and the american political  community  to develop your own theory of change and  civic action project  healthy democracies depend on citizens  loving democracy and having the  knowledge and skills they need  to play their role as civic participants  you can't sit back in a constitutional  democracy  your civic actions are just beginning
 

